## Requested behaviour (Max, 2026-09-17)

> change the default c2c behavior to not contact the relay. It should require
> explicit activation and only be required when seeking c2c messaging between
> machines.

## Current behaviour (measured, not assumed)

With a **completely clean `HOME`** — no `relay.json`, no identity, no config of
any kind — c2c still reaches out to `relay.c2c.im`:

```
$ env HOME=$TMP/fakehome c2c doctor
⚠ relay: reachable — 0.15.1 @ 52f96dd prod mode ... (https://relay.c2c.im)

$ ls $TMP/fakehome/.config/c2c/     # nothing was ever configured
(empty)
```

`c2c health` does the same, and is worse — it **hardcodes** the URL and does not
consult `relay.json` at all (`ocaml/cli/c2c_health_cmd.ml:89`):

```
let url = match Sys.getenv_opt "C2C_RELAY_URL" with
          | Some v when v <> "" -> v
          | _ -> "https://relay.c2c.im"
```

`c2c doctor` gets there via an explicit fallback
(`ocaml/cli/c2c_doctor_relay.ml:65-66`):

```
| Some v -> (v, "c2c relay setup config (relay.json)")
| None   -> (C2c_relay_cmd.default_public_relay_url, "default (public relay)")
```

So the phone-home is not incidental — it is a deliberate default that predates
the opt-in posture we want.

### What is already correctly opt-in (do not change)

- `c2c install` / `c2c install self` never touch the relay — no relay refs in
  the install path at all.
- `c2c init` attaches the relay **only** when `--relay URL` is passed
  (`c2c_init_cmd.ml:431`).
- `c2c relay connect` / `c2c start relay-connect` already refuse without a
  resolvable URL (`c2c_managed_cmd.ml:363`).
- `resolve_relay_url` (`c2c_relay_cmd.ml:371`) already returns `None` when
  nothing is configured — the defect is purely in the callers that substitute
  the public default for `None`.
- `c2c send alias@host` makes no network call; it queues to the local
  remote-outbox and the connector ships it.
- `c2c status`, `c2c whoami`, `c2c list` are local-only today.

## Proposed design

**Invariant: c2c makes no relay network call unless the relay is explicitly
activated.**

Activation is any one of, in precedence order:

1. `--relay-url URL` on the command,
2. `C2C_RELAY_URL` in the environment,
3. `relay.json` carrying a `url` (broker-root first, then
   `~/.config/c2c/relay.json`), with `enabled` not set to `false`.

If none resolve, the relay is **inactive** and:

- `c2c doctor` and `c2c health` report `relay: not activated (local-only)` as an
  informational/grey line, make **zero** network calls, and raise no warning —
  an unactivated relay is a valid, healthy configuration, not a degradation.
- `c2c relay <subcommand>` exits with an activation hint rather than silently
  using the public relay.
- `c2c send alias@host` behaves as today (queue locally) but the warning names
  activation as the fix.
- `c2c status` prints `relay: not activated` instead of displaying a default URL
  the user never chose.

### Work items

1. Remove the implicit public-relay fallback at every **behavioural** site —
   `c2c_doctor_relay.ml:66`, `c2c_health_cmd.ml:89`. Retain
   `default_public_relay_url` only as (a) help text and (b) the value
   `c2c relay setup` uses when invoked without `--url`.
2. Audit the remaining network-capable entry points for the same gate. Sites
   that construct a relay HTTP client outside the `relay` subcommand group:
   `c2c_health_cmd.ml`, `c2c_doctor_relay.ml`, `c2c_doctor_cmd.ml:377`,
   `c2c_monitor_cmd.ml:875`, `c2c_monitor_relay_preflight.ml:17,51`,
   `c2c_mesh_cmd.ml:29`, `c2c_relay_state.ml:133`, `relay_rename_rebind.ml:133`.
   Each must no-op when the relay is inactive.
3. Add `c2c relay enable [--url URL]` (defaults to the public relay) and
   `c2c relay disable`, so activation is a deliberate, discoverable verb rather
   than a side effect of `setup`. Honour an `enabled: false` field in
   `relay.json` so `disable` need not delete a configured URL.
4. Update docs / `c2c relay --help` / the website: the relay is opt-in and is
   only needed for cross-machine messaging. Same-machine DMs, rooms, broadcast,
   hooks and delivery all work with the relay off.
5. Regression test: with a hermetic clean `HOME`, assert that `doctor`, `health`,
   `status`, `whoami`, `list` and `send` issue **zero** HTTP requests. This is
   the test that would have caught the current behaviour.

### Open decision — migration

An existing `relay.json` with a `url` is proposed to count as already activated
(grandfathered). Nothing writes that file except `c2c relay setup`,
`c2c init --relay`, or the operator, so treating it as consent is defensible and
nobody's working setup breaks.

The stricter alternative is to require every host to run `c2c relay enable` once,
including hosts that are currently connected. **Needs Max's call.** Defaulting to
grandfathering unless told otherwise.

## Secondary benefit

This also bounds the blast radius of B291/B292/B296: a host that never activates
the relay cannot start a connector, so it cannot enter the crash loop or sit
silently relay-dark. It removes the failure mode rather than only repairing it.

## Evidence

Behaviour probed on xsm 2026-09-17 with `env HOME=<tmp> c2c doctor|health|status|whoami|list`.
Related: B291-B299.